  "motion": {
    "frames": 120,
    "note": "ours, modelled on Showdown's normal Golisopod idle (a subtle 39-frame breath). 120 frames = 3.6 s: 3 breaths (spine BREATH deg), the raised claw arms and forearms follow a beat later (FOLLOW, ARM). Signature claw flex, frames 66-104: the claw arms lift LIFT deg, the pincers ease open SNAP deg and snap shut in 6 frames, the forearms flex out FLEX deg, then settle (sin^2 / smootherstep easing). The claw flex (frames 66-105, exactly one breath long so the frames on either side match) is an intentional move beyond the idle: drawn per frame and left out of the idle's pop / flicker limits (style.fast_frames), like Glimmora's spin; every per-frame rule still applies."
  },
